{
  "ALG_DESC": "Calculation of slope-dependent accumulated cost surface, least-cost paths, and isolines from a point origin to one or more destinations. This function calculates the anisotropic accumulated cost of movement across the terrain, considering slope and various cost models. Version 4.1 - Ported to the movecost R package 3.1.0 (mc_* API: the cost surface is built once with mc_surface() and reused by every analysis; terra + sf + igraph core, ggplot2 plots). Requires the movecost R package >= 3.1.0. New in 4.1: the optional Terrain raster and Terrain Table (CSV with columns class,N) let the terrain factor N vary across the study area; the scalar N becomes the fallback for cells without a terrain value.",
  "Terrain": "Optional terrain-factor raster (movecost >= 3.1). Either a numeric raster whose cell values are the terrain factor N, or a categorical raster of class codes translated through the Terrain Table CSV. The scalar N parameter is the fallback for cells without a value; Inf makes a cell impassable. Cost functions that do not take a terrain factor warn when one is supplied.",
  "Terrain_Table": "Optional CSV file with columns 'class' and 'N' that translates the classes of a categorical Terrain raster into terrain factors. In R, mc_terrain_factors() returns the reference factors documented in mc_cost_functions() to help build this table.",
  "ALG_CREATOR": "Gianmarco Alberti",
  "ALG_HELP_CREATOR": "Enzo Cocca - adArte srl",
  "CRS": "Coordinate Reference System for the output layers.",
  "Area_of_interest": "Digital Terrain Model raster. If a polygon is provided, DTM will be downloaded from online sources for the area.",
  "Origin": "Starting point location from which the cost surface is calculated (point vector layer).",
  "Destination": "Destination point(s) to which least-cost paths are calculated (point vector layer).",
  "Barrier": "Optional barrier layer (line or polygon) representing areas where movement is restricted or has higher cost.",
  "PlotBarrier": "TRUE or FALSE - whether to display the barrier on the output plot.",
  "IrregularDTM": "Kept for compatibility and no longer needed: since movecost 3.0 NoData cells are excluded from the cost graph by construction, so paths and accumulated costs never cross them.",
  "Move": "Number of directions for cell connectivity: 4 (rook's case), 8 (queen's case), or 16 (knight and one-cell queen moves, default).",
  "Field": "Conductance value (0-1) assigned to barrier cells. 0 = impassable, 1 = no effect.",
  "Breaks": "Interval for isolines. If not specified, defaults to 1/10 of the cost surface range.",
  "Function": "Cost function to use:\n\n--- Walking time functions ---\n't' (default): Tobler's on-path hiking function\n'tofp': Tobler's off-path hiking function\n'mp': Marquez-Perez et al.'s modified Tobler\n'icmonp': Irmischer-Clarke (male, on-path)\n'icmoffp': Irmischer-Clarke (male, off-path)\n'icfonp': Irmischer-Clarke (female, on-path)\n'icfoffp': Irmischer-Clarke (female, off-path)\n'ug': Uriarte González\n'ma': Marín Arroyo\n'alb': Alberti (pastoral foraging)\n'gkrs': Garmy, Kaddouri, Rozenblat, Schneider\n'r': Rees\n'ks': Kondo-Seino\n'trp': Tripcevich\n\n--- Wheeled vehicles ---\n'wcs': Wheeled-vehicle critical slope\n\n--- Abstract cost ---\n'ree': Relative energetic expenditure\n'b': Bellavia\n'e': Eastman\n\n--- Metabolic energy ---\n'p': Pandolf et al.\n'pcf': Pandolf with correction factor\n'm': Minetti et al.\n'hrz': Herzog\n'vl': Van Leusen\n'ls': Llobera-Sluckin\n'a': Ardigo et al.\n'h': Hare",
  "Time": "Time unit for output: 'h' for hours (default), 'm' for minutes.",
  "Outp": "Output type: 'r' for raster (default), 'c' for contours only.",
  "Return_Base": "TRUE or FALSE - calculate and display least-cost paths back to the origin (dashed lines).",
  "Cognitive_Slope": "TRUE or FALSE - use cognitive/perceptual slope instead of real slope in calculations.",
  "Topo_Dist": "TRUE or FALSE (default FALSE). When TRUE, accumulated cost is calculated using topographic (surface) distance instead of planar distance, accounting for the extra distance incurred on sloped terrain (surface = planar * sqrt(1 + slope^2); a 30% slope adds about 4.4%, a 50% slope adds about 11.8%). Recommended for time-based hiking functions (Tobler etc.). Use with caution on metabolic energy functions, which were typically derived from planar measurements. Requires movecost R package >= 2.2.",
  "Critical_Slope": "Critical slope percentage (default: 10), typically 8-16. Used by wheeled-vehicle cost function.",
  "Walker_Body_Weight": "Walker's body weight in kg (default: 70). Used by Pandolf's and Van Leusen's functions.",
  "Carried_Load_Weight": "Weight of carried load in kg (default: 0). Used by Pandolf's and Van Leusen's functions.",
  "N": "Terrain coefficient representing ease of movement (default: 1). Higher values = harder terrain.",
  "Speed": "Walking speed in m/s (default: 1.2). Used by some metabolic functions.",
  "Zoom_Level": "Zoom level for online elevation data (0-15, default: 9). Higher = more detail but slower.",
  "RL": "Line type for return paths (default: 2 = dashed).",
  "CL": "TRUE or FALSE - display contour labels on the accumulated cost surface.",
  "DL": "TRUE or FALSE - display cost labels at destination locations.",
  "CB": "Size of contour break labels (default: 0.6).",
  "CLL": "Size of least-cost path labels (default: 0.6).",
  "Output_Accumulation_Coast": "Output raster layer showing the accumulated cost surface.",
  "Output_Isoline": "Output vector layer containing cost isolines (isochrones).",
  "Output_LCP": "Output vector layer containing least-cost path(s) to destination(s).",
  "Output_LCP_Back": "Output vector layer containing least-cost paths back to origin.",
  "Output_W_Cost": "Output vector layer with destination points and their walking costs."
}